{"title":"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(bash_but_it_takes_less_than_3_minutes)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (bash but it takes less than 3 minutes)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bored student walks down a hall that contains a row of closed lockers, numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c2fa23f6d345eb6b967ae9416712eaecf7741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. He opens the locker numbered 1, and then alternates between skipping and opening each locker thereafter. When he reaches the end of the hall, the student turns around and starts back. He opens the first closed locker he encounters, and then alternates between skipping and opening each closed locker thereafter. The student continues wandering back and forth in this manner until every locker is open. What is the number of the last locker he opens?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On his first pass, he opens all of the odd lockers. So there are only even lockers closed. Then he opens the lockers that are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, leaving only lockers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91f008182b346dbfaa0724332cc808ef03b94c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526536f9428d19e993780cf2186c66fdb11942d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\pmod{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. Then he goes ahead and opens all lockers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/3719805ab0c2d28699c681e5e55286fe9d4fe64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod {8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, leaving lockers either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/364a57d90668bcce71db21f18db254d5e0f081d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\pmod {16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/106386662607a00f1c1598572b02ab75a98a722c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 \\pmod {16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />. He then goes ahead and opens all lockers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/106386662607a00f1c1598572b02ab75a98a722c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 \\pmod {16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, leaving the lockers either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d769c8644ac307dc279e72629b3a4f580ab8543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\pmod {32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab43138e98cfa7a7133b88e34307318e45a8773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 \\pmod {32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. He then goes ahead and opens all lockers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d769c8644ac307dc279e72629b3a4f580ab8543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\pmod {32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d29f70a3768f45dcaaebc3cc9d65ce0430f63464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 \\pmod {64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757ffe3a405f67262553f79459a8bea3c7bf3370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54 \\pmod {64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. He then opens <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757ffe3a405f67262553f79459a8bea3c7bf3370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54 \\pmod {64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb65980cdba25c64f43a43c1a8bf4b253bf9b2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 \\pmod {128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65b94862ae6c1ae7ba4d0b8e5700345d444514b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86 \\pmod {128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />. He then opens <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb65980cdba25c64f43a43c1a8bf4b253bf9b2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 \\pmod {128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> and leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134e120382b8508d8d08399c9a01141861848ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86 \\pmod {256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/5/e35d06809b0683e8e128b93724a9c6cb09b00a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$214 \\pmod {256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />. He then opens all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/5/e35d06809b0683e8e128b93724a9c6cb09b00a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$214 \\pmod {256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8f3bbb4acf93a54d947da384d4726a76a308a21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86 \\pmod {512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb26ac1cf6966c4d7bb1c0c09735b301669f4db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$342 \\pmod {512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />, leaving lockers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0bb784646a08c7cc7021cddabacbb7011820ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86, 342, 598$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1683095faa4016c75c2a6bf4c71639328d178b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$854$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, and he is at where he started again. He then opens <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c6169a64f8271966651402df19345f38ae0c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4df930bc514e2cdc08c462c45602b49f5280e7a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$598$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, and then goes back and opens locker number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1683095faa4016c75c2a6bf4c71639328d178b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$854$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, leaving locker number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26fd7f4479b69222611ab026dee877d9337ac8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{342}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> untouched. He opens that locker.\n</p><p>~edit made by Yiyj1: the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bbf9d404f8d030d6e43392b3d32e83f1f38428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97cc8fb71c5bada9de132765a76998fd3721529f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> are the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb9d06f515dbd3a02640eab967650521b65371d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nRefer to the chart below for a more detailed view of the lockers that are left CLOSED on each turn, assuming that the lockers are numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c2fa23f6d345eb6b967ae9416712eaecf7741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> from left (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />) to right (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/3012c102310cce02866357902b72d44a5cd82dec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\pmod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p>\n<pre>Note: The general form in this chart is written differently, in the same way as Yiyj1 edited, to emphasize that the modulus is multiplied by two each time he makes a pass because he skips every other locker. \n</pre>\n<p><br />\nNOTICE THE PATTERNS: the least numbered and the greatest numbered lockers each change every two passes. The modulus changes every two passes as well. This speeds up calculation greatly.\n</p><p><br />\nFor the first five passes:\n</p><p>\\begin{array}{lc}\n\\text{Least number} &amp; 2 &amp; 2 &amp; 6 &amp; 6 &amp; 22 \\\\\n\\text{Greatest number} &amp; 1024 &amp; 1022 &amp; 1022 &amp; 1014 &amp; 1014 \\\\\n\\text{General form} &amp; 0 \\bmod 2 &amp; -2 \\bmod 4 &amp; -2 \\bmod 8 &amp; -10 \\bmod 16 &amp; -10 \\bmod 32 \\\\\n\\text{Direction of next turn} &amp; L &amp; R &amp; L &amp; R &amp; L \\end{array}\n</p><p>For the next five passes:\n</p><p>\\begin{array}{lc}\n\\text{Least number} &amp; 22 &amp; 86 &amp; 86 &amp; 342 &amp; 342 \\\\\n\\text{Greatest number} &amp; 982 &amp; 982 &amp; 854 &amp; 854 \\\\\n\\text{General form} &amp; -42 \\bmod 64 &amp; -42 \\bmod 128 &amp; -170 \\bmod 256 &amp; -170 \\bmod 512 \\\\\n\\text{Direction of next turn} &amp; R &amp; L &amp; R &amp; L \\end{array}\n</p><p>~edit made by unhappyfarmer\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can also solve this with recursion. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44695d539b9d5c031d226f37975b8b065313b912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the last locker he opens given that he started with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> lockers. Let there be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> lockers. After he first reaches the end of the hallway, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/66877bd3ddd8dd7995544baee949cc4737866732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> lockers remaining. There is a correspondence between these unopened lockers and if he began with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/66877bd3ddd8dd7995544baee949cc4737866732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> lockers. The locker <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (if he started with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/66877bd3ddd8dd7995544baee949cc4737866732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> lockers) corresponds to the locker <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049780b1c382a15bc5271a55ec0adfcf835313d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n+2-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" /> (if he started with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> lockers). It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c87a031d161cdf78ae07200eb069c8d018fe2f4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{n} = 2^{n} +2 -2L_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"163\" height=\"15\" /> as they are corresponding lockers. We can compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/abad337fec833414b4beda6be65d3d61684979d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and use the recursion to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14c35422536e2d3061501304a29fd2dcf9feec5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{10}=\\boxed{342}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><br />\nI will illustrate this solution with a small example, and solving using a slightly different way taken from the first solution found on the Random Math Wiki page for this problem. Take for example if there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> numbers: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/391d636221728fea9f3557adb294dfd277f5ff28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1 , 2 , 3 , 4]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" />. After the first pass, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d8fd14e4ba59fbd9c193191e53cb9678f7a0892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2/2 = 2^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" /> numbers left: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3f959e21da89be8ad3dabb689ff09b09c041699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[2 , 4]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />. Dealing with the new set on the second pass corresponds exactly to dealing with the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef45891fb1ae1cecfbfe2067492be5733fbb3aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1 , 2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> going from right to left (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b28c026b72a20eefa82746aa6b0c6879d464de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[2 , 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />), and we know that the last remaining locker of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef45891fb1ae1cecfbfe2067492be5733fbb3aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1 , 2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the original set. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the bijection corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the original set after one pass, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (bijection) with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In general terms, each number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f275b1f33e3c37ece0e41964f0bcb806e95b46b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> because half the numbers are taken out in one pass, but you need to reverse the order of the new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4f26614a4233b3c4b29e6e33a1729227be3cc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k-1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> numbers so each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79cfd6aa00c49c25232c973685b7e7f4edf65305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k-1} + 1 - \\frac{n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"34\" /> and because we consider the last number left after passing, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23ea93f59b29e7437d1489ce007bfe8fa446a391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{k-1} = 2^{k-1} + 1 - \\frac{L_k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"39\" /> and because we want the original number that the bijection corresponds to, rearrange to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201fb00d7259579e0e6f0f0d9879852c232bae2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{k} = 2^{k} +2 -2L_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />. We know the last number (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119ec649912d4b7db5ec52211bb001258098e858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />) of very small sequences (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), so for the doubled sequence the last number is the number that corresponds with the small sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then do recursion like the above solution states.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(bash)\">Solution 3 (bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>List all the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c2fa23f6d345eb6b967ae9416712eaecf7741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, then do the process yourself!!! It will take about 25 minutes (if you don't start to see the pattern), but that's okay, eventually, you will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26fd7f4479b69222611ab026dee877d9337ac8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{342}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>(Note: If you try to do this, first look through all the problems! -Guy)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28bash_but_it_takes_less_than_3_minutes.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(bash_but_it_takes_less_than_3_minutes)\">Solution 4 (bash but it takes less than 3 minutes)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (bash but it takes less than 3 minutes)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that whenever the student makes a pass starting on one end, the number at the other end of that line will remain. This is very important.\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/3/333d8f49965fe5486448c95eca1215808cdd84a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,4...,1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba8796fa063909d5fd96ff66c9924479532a2812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,4,6,...,1022, 1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (reversed, note that we take the second-to-last term of the previous sequence for every new sequence):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f65ad74857101985c23fefe1188c03665a95a4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1022, 1018,...,(2+4), 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183db2ee3defcf76ecd37e78d5ac82243ebdb309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, (6+4+4),...,(1022-4-4), 1022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"294\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed5861b14a4a27a8e3320dd2974a291d543126a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1014, (1014-16),..., (6+16), 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"249\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f3521aba64f144d3851ba4816ea456448b8b284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22, (22+32),..., (1014-32), 1014$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"267\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3e6fdf69001a94b65ddeb1d9be4bba2472b75a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$982, (982-64),..., (22 + 64), 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"249\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259e780ffa8ba6b802ee80ada44406b356e93ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86, (86+128),..., (982-128), 982$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"267\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb1f93e2a53a9d12338e4384a550f5a14f35434d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$854, (854-256),..., (86+256), 86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"267\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b982fe82bbc96ec52ca1718e6fa7c8285656988.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$342, (342+512)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dce71f61646178b18a8f7c70a35c3b6bccaf518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$342$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>The answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e272443cc3e368ac75469d37fc5c4435c8fdd2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{342}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"45\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~martianrunner\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Edit from EthanSpoon, Doing this with only even numbers will make it faster.\nYou'll see.\n02496\n</p><p>Edit from Iamaimogoldmedalist. Doing some few rounds in your head till you get Multiples of 4 or possibly numbers of the form 8k+2 will enhance your speed.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME\" title=\"1996 AIME\">1996 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1996 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181946\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.066 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.086 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 577/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1768/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 90/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17604/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.223      1 -total\n 61.72%    9.395      1 Template:AIME_box\n 35.90%    5.465      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2984:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017181946 and revision id 284545. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}